tempora.command.lookup.description=Shows the latest events around you and draws them in the world. Every filter is optional and they can go in any order. By default it searches 10 blocks around you, over the last 3 days, in every logger. Loggers that aren't tied to a place, such as weather, are shown by /tempora global instead.
tempora.command.lookup.arg0=How many blocks around you to search, default 10.
tempora.command.lookup.arg1=How far back to look, e.g. 30m, 6h, 1d, 2w, default 3d.
tempora.command.lookup.arg2=Which loggers to search, comma separated, e.g. break,place. Default is every logger.
tempora.command.lookup.header=%s %s %s
tempora.command.lookup.header.count=(%s)
tempora.command.lookup.header.latest=(latest %s)
tempora.command.lookup.header.hover=Click to search only %s.

# Loggers, as lookups show them: their name, and on hovering [Info], what they record and how the server has them set up.
# Another mod's logger adds its own tempora.logger.<logger name>.name and .description to its lang file.
