tempora.command.global.description=Shows the latest events from loggers that aren't tied to a place, such as weather and TPS. Works from anywhere, including the server console. Every filter is optional and they can go in any order. By default it shows the last 10 events of each, over the last 3 days.
tempora.command.global.arg0=How far back to look, e.g. 30m, 6h, 1d, 2w, default 3d.
tempora.command.global.arg1=Which loggers to show, comma separated, e.g. weather,tps. Default is every one.
tempora.command.global.arg2=How many events to show from each logger, up to 100, default 10.
tempora.command.global.nothing_found=Nothing was logged in the last %s.
tempora.command.global.positional_logger=%s records events at a place, use %s to look them up around you.

tempora.command.home.description=Finds the chunk a player has spent the most time in, from their movement history. Useful for finding their base.
tempora.command.home.arg0=Name of the player to look up.
tempora.command.home.arg1=Optional. Only use movement from this far back, e.g. 1mo, 2w.
tempora.command.home.arg2=Optional. Only look in this dimension.
tempora.command.home.result=Player %s is most active in dim %s, click %s to visit location.
tempora.command.home.unknown_player=No player called '%s' has joined this server.
tempora.command.home.no_db=Movement logging is disabled, so there is no movement history to search.
tempora.command.home.no_data=No movement data found for that query.

tempora.command.sql.description=Runs a read-only SELECT query against a logger's database and shows the results in chat, for investigations /tempora lookup can't express.
tempora.command.sql.arg0=A read-only SELECT query. The table name is the full logger name, e.g. PlayerMovementLogger.
tempora.command.sql.select_only=Only SELECT queries are allowed.
tempora.command.sql.missing_columns=Query missing required columns: %s
tempora.command.sql.missing_columns.advice=It is highly recommended to use SELECT * instead of specifying columns.
tempora.command.sql.no_results_in=No results found in %s.
tempora.command.sql.error=SQL Error: %s.
tempora.command.sql.query_quantity=Found %s matching results.
tempora.command.sql.query_quantity_if_max=Showing the first %s results (server limit: %s). Additional matches may be hidden.
tempora.command.sql.invalid_table=The query must name a logger table: %s.

